A||||2||wreakhavoc||4-speed linkage adjustment?||||1||
Z||000000||wreakhavoc||07-08-2001||06:53 PM||||<BR>After disassembling the linkage and disconnecting the shifter cables from the linkage to replace a broken bracket now I can't shift at all in 1st or 2nd shifter position and it shifts into 1st and 2nd gear in the 3rd and 4th shifter positions.  Being a novice I must have missed a step putting it all back together.  Any ideas? The Hayne's manual isn't much help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Steve Normington||07-08-2001||07:37 PM||||It sounds like your shift selector cable is not adjusted correctly. The cable you want to adjust is the one where the bolt points more towards the trunk. I think that you should move this bolt closer to the center of the car to fix this (if that doesn't work, try moving it the other way). The other bolt (the one that points up) controls the shifting from 1 to 2 or from 3 to 4. I think you can ignore this one.||||reg||1
Z||000002||wreakhavoc||07-08-2001||11:21 PM||||That worked. Thanks Steve!||||reg||1
